# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

    # Identify the information needed for the get-item process.
    SET current_room
    SET room_item to item located in current_room
    SET inventory to player's current inventory

    # Prompt for and receive the player's get-item command.
    OUTPUT "Enter your move:"
    INPUT player_command

    # Check whether the requested item is available in the current room.
    IF player_command equals "get " + room_item

        # Add the item to the player's inventory.
        ADD room_item to inventory
        OUTPUT room_item + " retrieved!"

        # Remove the collected item from the current room.
        SET room_item to NONE

    ELSE

        # Tell the player that the requested item cannot be collected.
        OUTPUT "Can't get that item!"

    ENDIF

    # Return to the main gameplay loop.
    CONTINUE game_loop

END get_item


